# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/scandals.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event scandal_ledger_lie
# en: The Dragon, Checked
title [06d544] = 那条龙，查证了
# en: Somebody has checked the Ledger's profile of you, the one with the better version of yourself in it. A boxed item on page two lists, very politely, the four things in it that never happened, with dates. The refectory has read it. Everybody is waiting to see what you'll say.
text [f17335] = 有人查证了《纪事报》对你的那篇专访，就是那篇写了一个更好的你的。第二版上一个方框里，非常客气地列出了其中四件从没发生过的事，还附上了日期。膳堂里的人都读过了。大家都在等你怎么说。
# en: A newspaper spread out on a refectory table, a small boxed headline circled in red ink, a ring of students reading over each other's shoulders.
scene [93ba95] = 膳堂桌上摊开一份报纸，一个小方框标题被红墨水圈了出来，一圈学生你挤我我挤你地凑着看。
# en: Own every word of it
opt.own.label [5b53d2] = 每个字都认下来
# en: You write to the Ledger: yes, you embellished; yes, it was vanity; no, there was no dragon. Nessa prints it in full. People are unkind about it for a week, and then, slowly, they start to trust what you say again.
opt.own.say.1 [6364ba] = 你写信给《纪事报》：是的，你添油加醋了；是的，那是虚荣；不，根本没有龙。内莎全文照登。人们刻薄了一个星期，然后，慢慢地，又开始相信你说的话了。
# en: Insist it was all true
opt.deny.label [118a9c] = 坚称全是真的
# en: You insist, calmly and in detail, that every word was true, and you tell it so well that the boxed item starts to look petty. By Friday people have decided the checker had a grudge. You don't feel as good about it as you'd hoped.
opt.deny.say.1 [d7af2d] = 你冷静而详细地坚称每个字都是真的，而且讲得那么好，让那个方框显得小家子气。到周五，人们认定查证的人是在报私仇。你并没有想象中那么痛快。
# en: You insist it was all true, and the checker produces a fifth thing, the one you'd forgotten. It's in the next issue, with your denial printed beside it. Nessa doesn't speak to you for a fortnight.
opt.deny.say.2 [4c04e9] = 你坚称全是真的，查证的人又拿出了第五件事，那件你自己都忘了的。它登在了下一期，旁边印着你的否认。内莎两个星期没跟你说话。
# en: Say Nessa twisted your words
opt.spin.label [acfa9a] = 说内莎歪曲了你的话
# en: You tell people the Ledger must have muddled your interview. It works, mostly: the story becomes one about sloppy journalism. Nessa reads it in silence, folds the paper very small, and doesn't ask you for another interview.
opt.spin.say.1 [d72057] = 你告诉别人，肯定是《纪事报》把你的采访弄混了。这招大体管用：故事变成了一个关于草率新闻的故事。内莎默默读完，把报纸折得很小，再也没请你做过采访。

@event scandal_candle_smoke
# en: The Study Candle Fire
title [db611e] = 学习蜡烛失火
# en: One of the candles with your face on it set a dormitory curtain smouldering last night. Nobody was hurt, but the whole tower was woken and stood in the courtyard in their nightclothes for an hour. By breakfast the castle is calling them "the {player} candles", and it isn't meant kindly.
text [1f93a0] = 昨晚，一支印着你的脸的蜡烛把宿舍的窗帘烧得冒了烟。没人受伤，可整座塔的人都被叫醒，穿着睡衣在庭院里站了一个小时。到早饭时，城堡里都管它们叫“{player}蜡烛”，可不是什么好话。
# en: A dormitory window with a scorched curtain, a smoking candle stub on the sill with a little painted label of a student's face, a prefect writing in a notebook.
scene [7b894a] = 宿舍的窗户上挂着烧焦的窗帘，窗台上放着一截冒烟的蜡烛头，上面贴着一张画有学生面孔的小标签，一位级长在本子上记录。
# en: Pay for the damage and stop the sales
opt.own.label [50417a] = 赔偿损失，停止售卖
# en: You go to the chandler and tell him to stop selling them, and you pay for the curtain out of your own cut. It costs you most of what you made. The tower grumbles, then forgives you, and someone leaves a fire bucket outside your door as a joke.
opt.own.say.1 [d37f7a] = 你去找蜡烛匠，让他别再卖了，又用自己的分成赔了窗帘。这花掉了你挣的大部分钱。整座塔的人抱怨了一阵，然后原谅了你，还有人开玩笑地在你门口放了一桶灭火的水。
# en: Prove the candle wasn't the cause
opt.deny.label [1acdf3] = 证明不是蜡烛的问题
# en: You take the stub to the alchemy laboratory and prove, with a great deal of smoke, that it was knocked over by a cat, not faulty. The cat belongs to a prefect. The story changes very fast.
opt.deny.say.1 [d73bd0] = 你把蜡烛头拿到炼金实验室，冒着一大股烟证明了它是被一只猫碰倒的，而不是蜡烛本身有毛病。那只猫是一位级长的。故事一下子就变了。
# en: You set out to prove the candle wasn't to blame, and your test sets a second curtain alight, in the laboratory, in front of the lecturer. The story is now much better than it was. You are not in it as the hero.
opt.deny.say.2 [39da70] = 你想证明不是蜡烛的错，结果你的实验在实验室里、当着讲师的面又点着了第二块窗帘。这下故事比原来精彩多了。而你在里面可不是英雄。
# en: Blame the chandler's wicks
opt.spin.label [236a27] = 怪蜡烛匠的灯芯
# en: You say, loudly and often, that the chandler must have changed his wicks without telling you. The castle turns on the chandler, who loses his academy trade for a term. You keep your name. You don't buy candles in the village for a long while.
opt.spin.say.1 [84e29c] = 你逢人便大声说，一定是蜡烛匠偷偷换了灯芯没告诉你。整个城堡都转而攻击蜡烛匠，他丢了学院一个学期的生意。你保住了名声。很长一段时间里，你都没再去村里买蜡烛。

@event scandal_memoir_book
# en: Chapter Nine
title [9d88a6] = 第九章
# en: The memoir has come out in full, and chapter nine, which you never read, says that you once copied a whole essay from a friend in your first year. It isn't true. It's very well written. Half the castle has a copy, and the other half is borrowing one.
text [7670e7] = 回忆录全本出版了，而你从没读过的第九章写道，你一年级时曾经从一个朋友那里抄了一整篇论文。这不是真的。可写得非常好。半个城堡的人都有一本，另一半正在借。
# en: A thin, glossy book lying open on a library table, one page heavily underlined, a group of students crowded around it whispering.
scene [55927d] = 图书馆桌上摊着一本薄薄的、光鲜的书，有一页被画满了线，一群学生围在旁边窃窃私语。
# en: Own that you never read it
opt.own.label [a988b0] = 承认你从没读过它
# en: You admit, publicly, that you signed a book you never read, and that chapter nine is invented. People laugh at you for it, and then believe you. The publisher's next printing quietly leaves the chapter out.
opt.own.say.1 [5263b1] = 你公开承认，你签了一本自己从没读过的书，第九章是编造的。人们为此笑话你，然后相信了你。出版社重印时悄悄删掉了那一章。
# en: Make the publisher retract it
opt.deny.label [04ef46] = 让出版社撤回
# en: You write to the publisher, then go to the city and sit in his office until he agrees to print a correction and pay you for the trouble. The correction is small. The money is not. The castle decides you were wronged.
opt.deny.say.1 [a2f725] = 你写信给出版社，又去了城里，坐在他的办公室里不走，直到他同意刊登更正并赔偿你的麻烦。更正很小。赔偿可不小。城堡里的人认定你受了冤枉。
# en: The publisher points to the contract you signed, the clause about "creative licence", and offers you a free copy. You pay for the journey home yourself. The chapter stays in.
opt.deny.say.2 [216192] = 出版人指了指你签过的合同里那一条“创作自由”的条款，送了你一本免费的书。回家的路费是你自己掏的。那一章留了下来。
# en: Hint that someone else copied
opt.spin.label [c42b7e] = 暗示抄袭的另有其人
# en: You say, with a sad look, that it must have been confused with somebody else's story. Within a day, the castle has decided whose. It wasn't them either. They don't speak to you again.
opt.spin.say.1 [c3615e] = 你带着一脸遗憾说，那一定是和别人的故事弄混了。不到一天，城堡里就认定了是谁。那也不是他们干的。他们再也没跟你说过话。

@event scandal_flourish_hurt
# en: The {player}, Done Badly
title [16868f] = “{player}式”，做砸了
# en: A first-year doing "the {player}", the flourish that does nothing, did it so hard that the spell went off sideways. Nobody is badly hurt: the first-year has lost both eyebrows and is enjoying the attention. But a professor has written to the headmistress, and the word going round is "reckless".
text [39907b] = 一个一年级生做“{player}式”，就是那个毫无用处的花式，用力过猛，法术朝旁边炸了出去。没人伤得严重：那个一年级生的两道眉毛没了，正享受着大家的关注。可一位教授给院长写了信，到处都在传“鲁莽”这个词。
# en: An infirmary bed with a first-year sitting up, both eyebrows missing and one sleeve singed, a matron frowning, a crowd of first-years peering round the door.
scene [1b8b75] = 医务室的病床上坐着一个一年级生，两道眉毛都没了，一只袖子烧焦了，护士长皱着眉，一群一年级生从门边探头张望。
# en: Visit them and teach the real one
opt.own.label [b14aa7] = 去看望，教真正的花式
# en: You go to the infirmary and sit with the first-year, then teach the whole yard the real flourish, the one that steadies a cast, slowly, for a week. The eyebrows grow back. The professor's letter, you hear, ends with "and the student took it in hand."
opt.own.say.1 [2d6e0d] = 你去医务室陪那个一年级生坐了一会儿，然后花了一个星期，慢慢地教整个练习场那个真正的、能让施法更稳的花式。眉毛长回来了。你听说，那位教授的信最后写的是：“那个学生把事情管起来了。”
# en: Say it was never your flourish
opt.deny.label [41954f] = 说那从来不是你的花式
# en: You point out, reasonably, that you have never once done the flourish and that it isn't yours to teach or stop. People see the sense in it. The first-year, eyebrowless, agrees cheerfully that it was "more of a tribute".
opt.deny.say.1 [c76a80] = 你合情合理地指出，你从没做过那个花式，那不是你能教或能禁的。大家觉得有道理。那个没了眉毛的一年级生高高兴兴地同意，那“更像是一种致敬”。
# en: You say it was never your flourish, and somebody produces a sketch of you doing it, solemnly, in the yard, on the day the whole yard cheered. You had forgotten that. Nobody else has.
opt.deny.say.2 [7fa6df] = 你说那从来不是你的花式，结果有人拿出一张速写，画的正是你在练习场上郑重其事地做那个花式，就是整个练习场欢呼的那天。你早忘了。别人可没忘。
# en: Blame the lecturer who never stopped it
opt.spin.label [3e01bf] = 怪从没制止的讲师
# en: You ask, in the right ears, why the practice-yard lecturer let a dangerous flourish go on for a month. The lecturer is spoken to. The flourish is banned. You were never mentioned, and you never quite look the lecturer in the eye again.
opt.spin.say.1 [527e8f] = 你在该说的人耳边问了一句：为什么练习场的讲师让一个危险的花式流行了一个月？讲师被约谈了。花式被禁了。从头到尾没人提到你，而你再也没能正眼看那位讲师。

@event scandal_wrong_notes
# en: The {player} Method, Failed
title [2e7e39] = “{player}学习法”，失败了
# en: The copies of your notes that were sold in the common room had a mistake in them, in a page you never corrected, and a first-year who learned it word for word has failed a paper on it. The first-year's friends are telling everyone that "the {player} method" is a fraud, and that you took money for it.
text [fe537c] = 公共休息室里卖的那些你的笔记抄本有个错误，就在你从没改过的一页里，一个一年级生一字不差地背下来，结果一门考试没过。那个一年级生的朋友们逢人就说“{player}学习法”是骗人的，还说你收了钱。
# en: A results list pinned to a board, a first-year in tears beside it clutching a sheaf of copied notes, older students reading the notes and shaking their heads.
scene [cd260a] = 布告板上钉着成绩单，一个一年级生攥着一沓抄来的笔记在旁边哭，几个年长的学生读着那些笔记直摇头。
# en: Refund it and tutor the first-year
opt.own.label [d4d20a] = 退钱，辅导那个一年级生
# en: You give back every crown you made, and spend three evenings with the first-year going over the paper properly. They pass the resit. The first-year's friends, grudgingly, stop telling the story, and start telling a different one.
opt.own.say.1 [d46b3d] = 你把挣来的每一个克朗都退了回去，又花了三个晚上和那个一年级生好好过了一遍那门课。对方补考过了。那个一年级生的朋友们不情不愿地不再讲那个故事，开始讲另一个了。
# en: Point out the page wasn't yours
opt.deny.label [4dd309] = 指出那一页不是你写的
# en: You find the original and show, page by page, that the mistake was added by the copyist. It's true, and it's convincing. The seller has to refund everyone. You still feel bad about the first-year.
opt.deny.say.1 [c89be3] = 你找出原稿，一页一页地证明那个错误是抄写的人加上去的。这是真的，也很有说服力。卖家只好给所有人退钱。你还是为那个一年级生感到难过。
# en: You go looking for your original, and find the mistake in your own hand. There's no arguing with it. The story gets worse for the week you spent pretending it wasn't there.
opt.deny.say.2 [cd42bc] = 你去找你的原稿，结果在你自己的笔迹里找到了那个错误。这没法争辩。你装作没这回事的那个星期，让故事变得更糟了。
# en: Blame the seller
opt.spin.label [70953e] = 怪卖家
# en: You tell everyone the third-year with the cash tin had been altering the notes for profit. The third-year is hauled in front of a prefect and loses their place in two clubs. It isn't quite true. It's close enough that you sleep, most nights.
opt.spin.say.1 [887c53] = 你告诉所有人，那个捧着钱匣的三年级生为了赚钱一直在篡改笔记。那个三年级生被拉到级长面前，丢了两个社团的位置。这不完全是真的。但也差不多，所以大多数夜里你睡得着。

@event scandal_thornwick_cheat
# en: Thornwick Cries Foul
title [3ad11a] = 荆木喊犯规
# en: Thornwick's student paper says you cheated at the boundary stones: that the last spell, the one that won it, used a ward Thornwick rules forbid. It's half true. Lumenhold's rules allow it; Thornwick's don't, and nobody agreed whose rules it was. The cartoon on their front page is very good.
text [0c385c] = 荆木的校报说你在界石旁作弊了：说最后那个赢下比赛的法术用了荆木规则禁止的结界。这有一半是真的。流明堡的规则允许；荆木的不允许，而当时谁也没说好用谁的规则。他们头版上的漫画画得非常好。
# en: A rival school's newspaper held up in a courtyard, its front page showing a cartoon of a student cheating at a stone circle, a crowd jeering and laughing.
scene [153841] = 庭院里有人举着一份对手学校的报纸，头版漫画画的是一个学生在石阵边作弊，一群人起哄大笑。
# en: Offer them a rematch, their rules
opt.own.label [53b7ab] = 提出重赛，按他们的规则
# en: You write and offer a rematch under Thornwick rules, and win that too, by a hair. Thornwick's paper prints a short, sour correction. The cartoon goes up on the Lumenhold common-room wall, framed, with a new caption.
opt.own.say.1 [3b21ad] = 你写信提出按荆木的规则重赛，结果又赢了，险胜。荆木的校报登了一则简短而酸溜溜的更正。那幅漫画被裱了起来，挂在流明堡公共休息室的墙上，配上了新的说明文字。
# en: You offer a rematch under Thornwick rules, and lose it, fairly. It hurts. But the story Thornwick tells now is about a Lumenhold student who came back to lose properly, and it isn't an unkind one.
opt.own.say.2 [e0fcb6] = 你提出按荆木的规则重赛，然后公平地输了。很痛。可荆木如今讲的故事，是一个流明堡学生回来堂堂正正地输了一场，而这并不是个刻薄的故事。
# en: Say the rules were always Lumenhold's
opt.deny.label [9ba7ec] = 说规则一直是流明堡的
# en: You say flatly that the contest was at Lumenhold's boundary and under Lumenhold's rules. It's a fair point. It makes no difference to anybody at Thornwick, and it makes you sound, even to yourself, like someone who won on a technicality.
opt.deny.say.1 [6456b7] = 你断然表示，比赛在流明堡的地界上，按流明堡的规则进行。这有道理。可对荆木的任何人都毫无影响，而且连你自己听着都像个靠钻空子赢的人。
# en: Leak a Thornwick scandal of your own
opt.spin.label [a534b8] = 放出荆木自己的丑闻
# en: You find out something unflattering about the Thornwick student who sent the challenge, and make sure it reaches their paper's rival. Within a week, nobody at Thornwick is talking about the boundary stones. You won. It doesn't taste of much.
opt.spin.say.1 [bfe070] = 你打听到了那个发来挑战的荆木学生的一件不光彩的事，确保它传到了他们校报的对头那里。不到一个星期，荆木就没人再谈界石的事了。你赢了。却没什么滋味。

@event scandal_society_dare
# en: In Your Name
title [c7a5bc] = 以你之名
# en: The {player} Society, the club of first-years with ribbons, held an initiation last night, and the dare was to climb to the third gargoyle "like {player} would". One of them got stuck there till dawn. The castle is saying the society is dangerous, and that you never told them to stop.
text [76d41e] = {player}协会，就是那群系着缎带的一年级生，昨晚办了一场入会仪式，挑战是“像{player}那样”爬到第三座石像鬼那儿。其中一个困在那里直到天亮。城堡里都说这个协会很危险，说你从没让他们停下。
# en: A castle rooftop at dawn, a small first-year clinging to a gargoyle, a crowd of prefects and a professor staring up from the courtyard below.
scene [4dfcf3] = 黎明时分的城堡屋顶，一个小个子一年级生紧抱着一座石像鬼，一群级长和一位教授在下面的庭院里仰头望着。
# en: Take responsibility for the society
opt.own.label [517f8e] = 为协会负起责任
# en: You go to the headmistress yourself and say it was your name, so it's your society, and you should have been paying attention. You write the society some rules. They are thrilled to have rules. Nobody climbs anything again.
opt.own.say.1 [951163] = 你亲自去见院长，说那是你的名字，所以那就是你的协会，你本该多留点心。你给协会定了几条规矩。他们有了规矩，高兴坏了。再也没人爬过任何东西。
# en: Say you never asked for a society
opt.deny.label [553d7b] = 说你从没要过什么协会
# en: You point out, gently, that you never asked for a society and have been to exactly one meeting. People agree that that's fair. The first-years are mortified. The first-year from the gargoyle sends you a note: "SORRY. Still worth it."
opt.deny.say.1 [fef747] = 你温和地指出，你从没要过什么协会，总共只去过一次聚会。大家都认为这说得公道。一年级生们羞愧难当。那个困在石像鬼上的一年级生给你送来一张字条：“对不起。还是值得。”
# en: You say you had nothing to do with it, and a first-year, very upset, shows everyone the minutes from the meeting you attended, with your signature. "We thought you'd want us to be brave," the minutes say. It's in the Ledger by Friday.
opt.deny.say.2 [ea3080] = 你说你和这事毫无关系，一个非常难过的一年级生给所有人看了你参加过的那次聚会的记录，上面有你的签名。“我们以为你会希望我们勇敢，”记录上写着。周五就上了《纪事报》。
# en: Blame the society's president
opt.spin.label [5aac6f] = 怪协会的会长
# en: You let it be known that the president had been running the society badly for months. The president resigns in tears. The society carries on without them. You don't go to the next meeting, or any of them.
opt.spin.say.1 [0085a7] = 你让人们知道，会长几个月来一直把协会管得一团糟。会长哭着辞了职。协会没有会长照样办了下去。你没去下一次聚会，以后也一次都没去。

@event scandal_leaked_letter
# en: Private Correspondence
title [bef85e] = 私人信件
# en: A private letter of yours, a long, frank one written to someone back home, has been printed in a gossip sheet. It isn't the Ledger: it's one of those single pages that appear on the boards overnight. In it you say what you really think of several people. They have all read it.
text [f870ef] = 你的一封私人信件，一封写给家乡某人的、长长的、毫无保留的信，被登在了一份八卦小报上。不是《纪事报》：是那种一夜之间出现在布告板上的单页小报。信里你说了你对好几个人的真实看法。他们全都读过了。
# en: A gossip sheet with a letter printed across its centre, a student snatching a copy from a crowd, another reading it aloud on a bench.
scene [d1b4ff] = 一份八卦小报的正中间印着一封信，一个学生从人群里一把抢过一份，另一个坐在长凳上大声念着。
# en: Apologise to each of them, in person
opt.own.label [ba95e1] = 当面挨个道歉
# en: You go round, one by one, and apologise, and say the letter was unkind and you were tired and homesick when you wrote it. Most of them accept it. One of them says you were right about their singing. It takes a week, and it's the worst week of the term.
opt.own.say.1 [6a9198] = 你一个一个地去道歉，说那封信写得刻薄，写的时候你又累又想家。大多数人接受了。其中一个说你对自己唱歌的评价是对的。这花了一个星期，是这学期最难熬的一个星期。
# en: Find out who stole it
opt.deny.label [f1d3fa] = 查出是谁偷的
# en: You trace the paper and the ink back to a second-year with a grudge and a key to the post room. Once it's known the letter was stolen, the story becomes the thief's. People forgive you faster than you expected.
opt.deny.say.1 [3554a4] = 你顺着纸张和墨水追查到一个怀恨在心、又有收发室钥匙的二年级生。大家一知道信是被偷的，故事就成了小偷的故事。人们原谅你比你预想的快。
# en: You spend a week hunting the thief and find nothing, and meanwhile three more pages of the letter appear. Everybody has noticed that you never said it wasn't true.
opt.deny.say.2 [c486dc] = 你花了一个星期找小偷，什么也没找到，与此同时，那封信又冒出了三页。所有人都注意到，你从没说过信里的话不是真的。
# en: Say it was forged
opt.spin.label [204199] = 说信是伪造的
# en: You tell everyone the letter was forged, by someone who hates you, and you have a guess who. It works. Somebody else is now the most disliked student in the castle. You can't quite meet the eyes of the people in the letter.
opt.spin.say.1 [9d4695] = 你告诉所有人那封信是伪造的，出自某个恨你的人之手，而且你猜得到是谁。这招奏效了。如今城堡里最招人厌的学生换了别人。你没法直视信里提到的那些人的眼睛。

@event scandal_cheating_rumour
# en: Nobody Gets Marks Like That
title [aefd29] = 没人能考出那种分数
# en: Somebody has started saying that nobody gets marks like yours honestly, and that someone famous could easily get hold of the papers. It's nonsense. But the examiners have heard it, and you've been asked, very politely, to come and answer some questions on Thursday.
text [851417] = 有人开始说，没人能老老实实考出你那样的分数，一个名人要弄到考卷简直易如反掌。这是胡说。可考官们听到了，你被非常客气地请去周四回答几个问题。
# en: A corridor outside an examiners' office, students muttering behind their hands as one student passes with a results slip.
scene [071f03] = 考官办公室外的走廊里，一个学生拿着成绩单经过，旁边的学生们捂着嘴嘀嘀咕咕。
# en: Ask them to examine you again
opt.own.label [3041a5] = 请他们重新考你
# en: You ask the examiners to set you a fresh paper, there and then, with a proctor. They do. You sit it in a cold room with an hourglass and a lecturer watching, and you do well. The rumour dies in a week, and nobody apologises.
opt.own.say.1 [3ca702] = 你请考官们当场给你出一套新卷子，派人监考。他们照办了。你在一间冷冰冰的屋子里，对着沙漏、在一位讲师的注视下答完了卷子，考得很好。一个星期后谣言平息了，没人道歉。
# en: Answer their questions, and theirs alone
opt.deny.label [42580b] = 只回答他们的问题
# en: You answer every question on Thursday plainly and well, and the examiners thank you for your time. One of them says, at the door, that they'd never really doubted it. By the next week the rumour has moved on.
opt.deny.say.1 [869204] = 周四你把每个问题都答得平实而漂亮，考官们感谢你抽空前来。其中一位在门口说，他们其实从没真的怀疑过。到下一周，谣言就转到别处去了。
# en: You get flustered on Thursday, and the examiners, who had only half believed the story, start to believe it a little more. Nothing comes of it in the end. But it takes the whole term to come to nothing.
opt.deny.say.2 [4067e7] = 周四你慌了神，原本只信了一半的考官们开始多信了一点。最后什么也没查出来。可这件事花了整整一个学期才不了了之。
# en: Say who really had the papers
opt.spin.label [130194] = 说出真正拿到考卷的人
# en: You let slip a name, someone you once saw near the examiners' office. The rumour moves on to them at once. They are questioned for a week and cleared. They know where it came from. So do you.
opt.spin.say.1 [1ae636] = 你“不小心”说出了一个名字，一个你曾经在考官办公室附近见过的人。谣言立刻转到了对方身上。对方被问了一个星期的话，最后洗清了嫌疑。对方知道是谁起的头。你也知道。

@event scandal_ex_tells_all
# en: Their Side of It
title [f0d274] = 对方的说法
# en: {x} has been telling the story of the two of you to anyone who'll listen: the way it started, the way it ended, and a great many things in between that you'd thought were private. The common room goes quiet when you come in. Somebody coughs.
text [25ca30] = {x}一直在跟所有愿意听的人讲你们俩的故事：怎么开始的，怎么结束的，还有中间许多你以为是私事的事。你走进公共休息室时，里面安静了下来。有人咳嗽了一声。
# en: A crowded common room, a student holding court with a cup in hand, telling a story to a rapt circle, another student frozen in the doorway.
scene [e838be] = 拥挤的公共休息室里，一个学生端着杯子被一圈人围着，讲得眉飞色舞，另一个学生僵在门口。
# en: Tell your own side, kindly
opt.own.label [b968f1] = 和气地讲讲你的说法
# en: You don't argue. You say that it ended badly and you're sorry for your part in it, and that {x} isn't wrong about everything. It takes the air out of the story. A week later {x} stops you in a corridor and says, stiffly, that {they} had gone too far.
opt.own.say.1 [022604] = 你没有争辩。你说这段感情结束得很糟，你为自己那部分感到抱歉，而{x}也不是全都说错了。故事一下子泄了气。一个星期后，{x}在走廊里拦住你，生硬地说{they}说得过分了。
# en: Say it's all made up
opt.deny.label [5a0a8e] = 说全是编的
# en: You laugh it off and say {x} always did have an imagination. People decide to believe you, mostly. {x} hears about it and goes very quiet, and the story stops, and so does anything else between you.
opt.deny.say.1 [e31acb] = 你一笑置之，说{x}向来想象力丰富。人们大体上决定相信你。{x}听说后变得非常沉默，故事停了，你们之间的一切也停了。
# en: You say it's all made up, and {x} produces your letters. All of them. The common room reads them aloud, with feeling. You have to leave by the window.
opt.deny.say.2 [c53b03] = 你说全是编的，{x}拿出了你写的信。全部。公共休息室里的人声情并茂地念了出来。你只好从窗户溜走。
# en: Tell a worse story about {x}
opt.spin.label [23beff] = 讲一个关于{x}的更糟的故事
# en: You tell a story about {x}, a worse one, and some of it is true. The common room switches sides by supper. {x} doesn't come down to meals for a week. You win, in the sense that nobody's talking about you.
opt.spin.say.1 [81d5f3] = 你讲了一个关于{x}的故事，更糟糕的一个，其中有些是真的。到晚饭时，公共休息室里的人都倒向了你这边。{x}一个星期没下来吃饭。你赢了，就是说，没人再谈论你了。

@event scandal_curfew_column
# en: Seen Where You Shouldn't Be
title [b2f95b] = 出现在不该出现的地方
# en: The gossip column has a paragraph about a "certain famous student" seen creeping back past the night porter at two in the morning, "from the direction of the boathouse". Nobody needs to guess who. A prefect has torn it down twice. It keeps going back up.
text [9ff71a] = 八卦专栏里有一段写的是一位“某著名学生”凌晨两点“从船屋的方向”偷偷溜过守夜人身边。不用猜是谁。一位级长已经撕掉它两次了。它总是又被贴回去。
# en: A gossip column pinned to a noticeboard with one paragraph circled, a sketch beside it of a student creeping past a lantern at night.
scene [3b15a1] = 布告板上钉着一份八卦专栏，其中一段被圈了出来，旁边画着一个学生在夜里偷偷溜过一盏灯笼的速写。
# en: Own up to the prefects
opt.own.label [fdd226] = 向级长坦白
# en: You go to the prefects' room and say yes, it was you, and you were out walking because you couldn't sleep. They give you a week of detention polishing the trophy cabinet. It's dull. The column moves on, because there's nothing left to whisper.
opt.own.say.1 [8df111] = 你去级长室说，是的，是你，你睡不着，出去走走。他们罚你关一个星期禁闭擦奖杯柜。很无聊。专栏转向了别的话题，因为已经没什么可嘀咕的了。
# en: Prove you were somewhere else
opt.deny.label [40d6e9] = 证明你在别处
# en: You produce three friends who swear you were playing cards in the common room till one. The column prints a short, sniffy correction. Your friends make you buy them supper for a month.
opt.deny.say.1 [f96abc] = 你找来三个朋友，发誓说你一直在公共休息室打牌打到一点。专栏登了一则简短而傲慢的更正。你的朋友们让你请了一个月的晚饭。
# en: Your alibi lasts until somebody points out that the common room was locked at midnight. The next column runs the whole story, with the bit about the alibi. The prefects are not amused.
opt.deny.say.2 [fca442] = 你的不在场证明一直撑到有人指出，公共休息室午夜就锁门了。下一期专栏把整件事都登了出来，连带不在场证明那一段。级长们一点也不觉得好笑。
# en: Hint it was someone in a borrowed coat
opt.spin.label [a1c7a7] = 暗示那人穿着借来的外套
# en: You let it be known you'd lent your coat that night to a friend. It's half true. The column hunts for the friend, who doesn't thank you for it, and the story slowly turns into one about the coat.
opt.spin.say.1 [9b6602] = 你放出话说，那天晚上你把外套借给了一个朋友。这有一半是真的。专栏开始追查那个朋友，对方可一点也不感激你，故事慢慢变成了一件外套的故事。

@event scandal_snubbed
# en: The Snub
title [8360aa] = 冷落
# en: The story is that a first-year waited two hours in the rain outside your lecture to ask you something, and you walked straight past without a word. You don't remember it. You might have been thinking about something else. The first-year cried, apparently, and the first-years have decided you're a monster.
text [f57c34] = 传说一个一年级生冒着雨在你的课室外等了两个小时，想问你一件事，而你一言不发地径直走了过去。你不记得这回事。你可能当时在想别的事。据说那个一年级生哭了，一年级生们已经认定你是个怪物。
# en: A first-year sitting alone on a stone bench, face in hands, a group of first-years glaring across a courtyard at an older student walking away.
scene [18b961] = 一个一年级生独自坐在石凳上双手捂着脸，一群一年级生隔着庭院怒视着一个正在走开的年长学生。
# en: Find the first-year and apologise
opt.own.label [ea83ad] = 找到那个一年级生道歉
# en: You find the first-year and apologise, properly, and ask what they'd wanted to ask. It was about the library. You take them there. By the end of the week, the first-years' monster has become the first-years' favourite again, mostly.
opt.own.say.1 [3bcdbd] = 你找到那个一年级生，好好地道了歉，问对方当时想问什么。是关于图书馆的。你带对方去了。到周末，一年级生眼里的怪物又差不多变回了一年级生最喜欢的人。
# en: Say you were never there that day
opt.deny.label [f22d27] = 说那天你根本不在
# en: You point out that you were in the infirmary that afternoon with a cold, and the matron, when asked, agrees. It's true, as it happens. The first-year must have mistaken somebody else for you.
opt.deny.say.1 [b5c5e4] = 你指出那天下午你感冒了，在医务室，护士长被问到时也证实了。碰巧这是真的。那个一年级生一定是把别人错认成了你。
# en: You say you were never there, and three first-years say they saw you. The first-years are now sure you're a monster and a liar. It takes the rest of the term.
opt.deny.say.2 [467975] = 你说你根本不在，三个一年级生说他们看见你了。现在一年级生们确信你既是怪物又是骗子。这花了整个学期。
# en: Say the first-year has been stalking you
opt.spin.label [185821] = 说那个一年级生一直跟踪你
# en: You tell people, sadly, that the first-year has been following you everywhere, and you didn't know what to do. People are sympathetic. The first-year stops coming to meals for a while. You never find out what they'd wanted to ask.
opt.spin.say.1 [8089fd] = 你难过地告诉别人，那个一年级生一直到处跟着你，你不知道该怎么办。人们很同情你。那个一年级生有一阵子不来吃饭了。你始终不知道对方当时想问什么。

@event scandal_thornwick_defection
# en: Off to Thornwick?
title [cfa5d1] = 要去荆木了？
# en: Thornwick's student paper has run a story that you're leaving Lumenhold for Thornwick next year, with a quote, apparently from you, about Lumenhold's "draughty towers and draughtier lecturers". You've never said it. Half the castle believes it, and the other half is hurt that you'd joke about it.
text [f5a743] = 荆木的校报登了一篇报道，说你明年要离开流明堡去荆木，还附了一句据说是你说的话，说流明堡“塔楼漏风，讲师更漏风”。你从没说过。半个城堡的人信了，另一半为你竟然拿这个开玩笑而难过。
# en: A newspaper from a rival school pinned up in a courtyard, the headline in large red letters, Lumenhold students tearing it down while others stare.
scene [f61a99] = 庭院里钉着一份对手学校的报纸，标题是大大的红字，几个流明堡学生在撕它，其他人盯着看。
# en: Say you'd never leave
opt.own.label [62955d] = 说你永远不会走
# en: You stand up at supper and say, plainly, that you've never been asked and you'd never go, and that the towers are draughty but they're yours. The Great Hall bangs the tables. It's embarrassing. It works.
opt.own.say.1 [a520e1] = 你在晚餐时站起来，平平实实地说，从没人邀请过你，你也永远不会去，塔楼是漏风，但那是你的塔楼。大礼堂里的人拍起了桌子。很难为情。很管用。
# en: Prove the quote is fake
opt.deny.label [d11047] = 证明那句话是假的
# en: You find that the "quote" is lifted, word for word, from a Thornwick student's own letter home, which their paper printed last year. Lumenhold reprints both side by side. Thornwick's paper is very quiet for a month.
opt.deny.say.1 [9de418] = 你发现那句“引语”是一字不差地从一个荆木学生自己的家信里搬来的，那封信去年就登在他们的校报上。流明堡把两者并排重印了出来。荆木的校报安静了一个月。
# en: You try to prove the quote was invented, and can't, and the more you protest, the more people suspect you did say it, once, in a bad mood, somewhere. You probably did. You can't remember.
opt.deny.say.2 [e24aa6] = 你想证明那句话是编的，却证明不了，你越是抗议，人们越怀疑你确实说过，在某次心情不好的时候，在某个地方。你多半说过。你记不得了。
# en: Hint you've had a better offer
opt.spin.label [693c5d] = 暗示你有更好的去处
# en: You let it be known you've had offers from all sorts of places, and Thornwick isn't the best of them. People are impressed. They are also, now, a little bit wary of you, and stop telling you things.
opt.spin.say.1 [2e8264] = 你放出话说，你收到过各种地方的邀请，荆木还算不上最好的。人们很佩服。他们现在也对你有点戒心了，不再什么都告诉你。

@event scandal_forged_love_letter
# en: A Letter You Didn't Write
title [c36010] = 一封你没写过的信
# en: A love letter is going round the library, in what looks exactly like your handwriting, addressed to {y}. It is very passionate and very badly spelled. You didn't write it. {y} has read it, and is now going very carefully out of every room you come into.
text [a16a54] = 图书馆里正传着一封情书，笔迹看上去和你的一模一样，写给{y}。它非常热烈，拼写非常糟糕。你没写过。{y}读过了，现在只要你走进哪个房间，{they}就小心翼翼地从哪个房间出去。
# en: A pink letter being passed hand to hand along a library table, a student at one end turning bright red, another at the far end staring in horror.
scene [66e9c1] = 一封粉红色的信在图书馆的长桌上一个接一个地传着，桌子一头的学生满脸通红，另一头的学生惊恐地瞪着眼。
# en: Go and talk to {y} first
opt.own.label [f06f9c] = 先去找{y}谈谈
# en: You find {y} before anybody else can, and say you didn't write it and you're sorry {they} had to read it. {y} laughs, from relief. "I did wonder about the spelling." The story fizzles, and you and {y} are, oddly, closer for it.
opt.own.say.1 [8a6abd] = 你赶在别人之前找到{y}，说那不是你写的，很抱歉让{they}读到了那封信。{y}松了口气，笑了。“我确实怀疑过那拼写。”故事就这么没了下文，而你和{y}反倒因此更亲近了些。
# en: Find the forger
opt.deny.label [3df4bc] = 找出伪造者
# en: You compare the hand with every exercise book in your year, and find the forger: a second-year who thought it was the funniest thing ever done. The library agrees, a little. The second-year apologises, mostly to {y}.
opt.deny.say.1 [6d0f64] = 你把那笔迹和你们年级每一本练习簿比对，找到了伪造者：一个觉得这是史上最好笑的事的二年级生。图书馆里的人也有点同意。那个二年级生道了歉，主要是向{y}道歉。
# en: You can't find the forger, and the longer you look, the more people think you're covering for yourself. {y} starts taking the long way round the library. It's a month before you can laugh about it.
opt.deny.say.2 [847953] = 你找不到伪造者，找得越久，人们越觉得你在替自己打掩护。{y}开始绕远路去图书馆。过了一个月，你才能笑着提起这件事。
# en: Say it was meant for someone else
opt.spin.label [27d155] = 说那是写给别人的
# en: You say, with a wink, that it was meant for somebody else entirely, and wasn't it obvious? The castle spends a week guessing who. {y} is relieved, and then, for some reason, hurt, and you never quite work out why.
opt.spin.say.1 [2b87f9] = 你眨眨眼说，那封信其实是写给另一个人的，难道不明显吗？整个城堡猜了一个星期是谁。{y}松了口气，接着，不知为什么，又觉得受了伤，而你始终没弄明白为什么。

@event scandal_credit_taken
# en: Whose Idea Was It?
title [b99199] = 这是谁的主意？
# en: The idea everyone's praising you for, the one the lecturer called "the best thing this year", started as something {f} said to you over supper. You'd forgotten. {f} hadn't. Now {f}'s friends are telling everyone that the famous {player} steals ideas from people who aren't famous.
text [08215b] = 大家都在为之称赞你的那个点子，讲师说的“今年最好的东西”，最初是{f}在晚饭时跟你说的。你忘了。{f}可没忘。现在{f}的朋友们逢人就说，著名的{player}偷不出名的人的点子。
# en: A lecture hall with a diagram on the board, a professor pointing to one student, another student in the row behind sitting with arms folded and jaw set.
scene [586a85] = 阶梯教室的黑板上画着一张图，一位教授指着一个学生，后一排的另一个学生抱着胳膊，咬紧了牙。
# en: Give {f} the credit, out loud
opt.own.label [157334] = 大声把功劳归给{f}
# en: You go to the lecturer, with {f}, and say whose idea it was first. The lecturer puts both names on the board. {f} goes red and says it wasn't much of an idea, really. It was. People notice that you said so.
opt.own.say.1 [87ded9] = 你带着{f}去找讲师，说这个点子最先是谁想的。讲师把两个人的名字都写在了黑板上。{f}脸红了，说其实也算不上什么好点子。它是。人们注意到你说了实话。
# en: Say you'd had it too
opt.deny.label [0e8364] = 说你也想到过
# en: You say you'd been thinking along the same lines for weeks, and you have notes to prove it, nearly. People accept it. {f} doesn't, and things between you are cool for a long while.
opt.deny.say.1 [c6a5b1] = 你说你几个星期来一直在往这个方向想，还有笔记为证，差不多吧。人们接受了。{f}没有，你们之间冷了很长一段时间。
# en: You say you'd had the idea too, and {f} produces the napkin from supper with the idea sketched on it, and the date. The story is now much worse, and it has a napkin in it.
opt.deny.say.2 [b30f73] = 你说你也想到过，{f}拿出了那天晚饭时的餐巾，上面画着那个点子，还写着日期。现在故事糟糕多了，里面还有一张餐巾。
# en: Say {f} is jealous
opt.spin.label [c2f09d] = 说{f}是嫉妒
# en: You say, sorrowfully, that {f} has always been a little jealous of you. People believe it, because you're famous and {f} isn't. {f} stops sitting with you at supper, and you start to wonder whose ideas you're going to have now.
opt.spin.say.1 [4099d5] = 你沉痛地说，{f}一直有点嫉妒你。人们信了，因为你有名，而{f}没有。{f}不再和你一起吃晚饭了，你开始想，以后你的点子要从哪儿来。
